Z||000000||Phil||12-16-2000||08:43 PM||||Need to check a few things. The wife would really prefer an auto in her now 5 sp 88 coupe, I can get an auto from an 87 coupe. What do I have to change? Can I just use the chip from the 87 or do I need the ECM and are the axles the same? I'm not too savy on the 4 bangers.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif"> <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||12-16-2000||09:25 PM||||Trans, axles, radiator (and lines), shifter/cable, trans mounts, TV cable to throttle body, flexplate, torque converter and wiring (to ECM), backup light wiring, steering column lock, brake pedal, automatic chip (same ECM 1227170).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-16-2000||09:42 PM||||Thanks-kinda   I have access to a donor 87. I knew most of the stuff wasn't sure on the ECM and axles||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||12-16-2000||10:15 PM||||Maybe you should have your wife test drive an automatic fiero so that she could feel the difference between the two before you do the conversion. She may change her mind and after all that work that would really suck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||12-17-2000||08:03 AM||||She really doesn't care about power, I don't think she's ever nailed mine. She's just tired of shifting after about 40 years of driving.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||12-17-2000||09:42 AM||||i was looking into this swap myself to a 440 auto from my 4 speed. I was told that you need to replace the complete dash wiring harness too, or it wouldnt shift or cruise control work. estimate was over $4000 with a new crate 440 from Twin Cities Fiero. ill stick to my 4 spd i guess<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||12-17-2000||10:51 AM||||I think the 440 is electronic, where the TH125 isn't. That may be why you were told the dash wiring would have to be changed?||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||12-17-2000||12:41 PM||||A 440 is nothing but 125 with overdrive (and less reliability). The 4T60 is a newer 440. Neither are electronic. The 4T60E is electronic. <P>A 440 would be rather easy to install. It acts like a 125 with one more gear. 440's used heavier axles than the 125, but it wouldn't be a problem.  <P>Where the dash gets involved is beyond me. Maybe they mean the 4T60E (which makes no sense either). I'll bet they were refering to the complete ECM swap which would make you think the dash wiring changes. <P>Terry<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Master_Sushi||12-17-2000||10:15 PM||||Ill trade you for my 88 coupe auto  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> .||||reg||10
Z||000009||Old Lar||12-17-2000||10:38 PM||||Bob at Twin Lake Fiero is putting in a t440 in my 88 GT and it isn't $4K.  It comes from the early 90s Pontiac/Buicks.  Its a straight swap since it isn't electronic. Just an axle replacement.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||12-17-2000||10:56 PM||||Bob at Twin Lakes quoted me $2500 for a T440 trans. That was the price of the trans AND for him to install it! (haven't done it yet, I'm saving to have the 3.4L swap done at the same time)||||reg||1
Z||000011||william_thorniii||12-18-2000||11:28 AM||||Phil,<P>I would be more than happy to work out a trade on my 87 EC auto with 89K on her (owned her since 48K).  I could possibly even throw in an 88 cradle conversion kit.  Mine doesn't have any power goodies or a sunroof and could use a coat of paint.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000012||terryk||12-18-2000||11:46 AM||||The 440 is not electronic unless we consider the 3rd and 4th gear switches and TCC electronic. In that case, so is the 125. It has the same things. <P>GM doesn't consider them electronic. The 4T60 is just a newer designation of the 440. The 4T60E is electronic (that's what the E means). The 4T60E has TCC solenoid and a pulse width modulator control to softly engage the TCC. It also has shift solendoids that control the forward gear selection. They can't select PR or N though. The 4T65E added the shift quality controls.||||reg||1
